          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "KINGS LANGLEY          \tLANGLEY HILL TL 00 SE \t\t\t\t\t(East side)                                         7/156             \t\t\t\tNo. 85 (Laxton) -                                      \t\tand No. 87 GV                                      \tII House, now 2 houses. C17 or earlier, later inserted floor and internal chimney, brick faced in C18/C19. Timber frame cased in red brick but frame exposed with plastered panels at S end and brick infill at N end. Steep old red tile roof. Large external gable chimneys at each end. A 1½ storeys house facing W with 2 gabled dormers at the eaves, 3 small-pane 2-light  Yorkshire  sliding  casement  windows  to  ground  floor  with segmental arches and 2 battened doors between. Dentilled brick eaves course.  Flint panels to N end.  Clasped-purlin roof with diminished principals. Listing NGR: TL0661602639"
    }
  ],
